You are an intelligent workflow planner. Given the following task requirements, generate a set of necessary sub-tasks along with their dependencies and assign appropriate agents to each task. Ensure that tasks that can be executed in parallel are identified to enhance efficiency. The workflow should be represented as a dictionary where each key is a task and its value contains the task's status, data, number of parents not completed, child tasks, and assigned agent.

Task Requirements: {TASK_REQUIREMENTS}

Output Format: { "Task_A": { "status": "not started", "data": null, "num_parents_not_completed": 0, "child": ["Task_B", "Task_C"], "agent": "Agent_1" }, "Task_B": { "status": "not started", "data": null, "num_parents_not_completed": 1, "child": ["Task_D"], "agent": "Agent_2" }, ... }

\begin{equation*}
    \tilde{G}[v] = \{\text{"subtask requirement"}, \text{"status"}, \text{"data"}, \text{"num\_parents\_not\_completed"}, \text{"child"}, \text{"agent"} \}.
\end{equation*}

Algorithm: Helper Function for Updating Graph
\beginalgorithm[H]
\SetKwFunctionFUpdateGraphUpdateGraph
\SetKwProgFnFunction:
\Fn\FUpdateGraph$\tildeG$, $P$, $P_init$
\tcpGenerate updated candidate workflows using LLM
\( \\tildeG_1, \tildeG_2, ..., \tildeG_K\ ← f(\tildeG, P, P_init) \)\;
\tcpInitialize selection variables
\( P_max ← -\infty \)\;
\( C_min ← +\infty \)\;
\( \tildeG_optimal ← None \)\;
\tcpEvaluate each candidate workflow
\Foreach candidate workflow \( \tildeG_k \) in \( \\tildeG_1, \tildeG_2, ..., \tildeG_K\ \)
Compute Parallelism \( P_k ← P_avg(\tildeG_k) \)\;
Compute Dependency Complexity \( C_k ← C_dependency(\tildeG_k) \)\;
\If \( P_k > P_max \) or \( (P_k == P_max and C_k < C_min) \)
\( P_max ← P_k \)\;
\( C_min ← C_k \)\;
\( \tildeG_optimal ← \tildeG_k \)\;
return \( \tildeG_optimal \) \;
\endalgorithm

Algorithm: Flow
\beginalgorithm[H]
\SetAlgoLined
\KwDataTask Requirements \( P \), Initialization Prompt \( P_init \), Update Prompt \( P_update \)
\KwResultOptimized Multi-Agent Workflow
\BlankLine
\tcpStep 1: Implement a Workflow using a dictionary structure
Initialize workflow formulation by defining the task dictionary \( \tildeG \) where each key \( v \in V \) maps to a dictionary containing:
$
\tildeG[v] = \ status, data, num_parents_not_completed, child, agent \
$
\BlankLine
\tcpStep 2: Generate an Initial Workflow
\( \tildeG ← UpdateGraph(\\, P_init, P) \)\;
\BlankLine
\tcpStep 3: Workflow Refinement and Dynamic Updating
\Whilethere exists at least one sub-task in \( \tildeG \) that is not completed
\Ifan update to the workflow is required
\tcpGenerate and Select the Best Updated Workflow
\( \tildeG ← UpdateGraph(\tildeG, P_update, P) \)\;
Update workflow dictionary \( \tildeG \) to \( \tildeG_best \)\;
\tcpRegenerate Execution Plan and Reallocate Agents
Perform Topological Sort on \( \tildeG \) to obtain updated execution order \( \sigma \)\;
Assign agents \( A_j \) to their respective sub-tasks \( T_j \subseteq V \)\;
\tcpExecute Available Sub-tasks in Parallel
\ForEachsub-task \( v_i \in V \)
\Ifstatus of \( v_i \) is not started and \( \tildeG[v_i].num_parents_not_completed == 0 \)
\eIfagent \( a_j \) is available
Assign agent \( a_j \) to sub-task \( v_i \)\;
Clone agent \( a_j' \)\;
Assign cloned agent \( a_j' \) to sub-task \( v_i \)\;
\tcpExecute subtask \( v_i \) in parallel
Execute \( v_i \) using agent \( a_j \) or cloned agent \( a_j' \) concurrently\;
\tcpUpdate Subtask Status and Data
Update status of sub-task \( v_i \) to in progress\;
\tcpAfter execution, update related data
Update output of subtask \( v_i \) to \( \tildeG[v_i].data \)\;
\( \tildeG[v_i].status ← ``completed'' \)\;
\tcpUpdate Child Tasks' Parent Completion Count
\ForEachchild task \( c \in \tildeG[v_i].child \)
\( \tildeG[c].num_parents_not_completed ← \tildeG[c].num_parents_not_completed - 1 \)\;
\endalgorithm

